  "summary_en": "Part 1 of Title 14 CFR sets out the FAA's general definitions, abbreviations and rules of construction for aviation regulation. Its only embodied-robotics content is the definitions of unmanned aircraft, small unmanned aircraft (under 55 pounds) and small UAS, which underpin the drone rules elsewhere in the chapter.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines 'unmanned aircraft' as an aircraft operated without the possibility of direct human intervention from within or on the aircraft.",
   "Defines 'small unmanned aircraft' as weighing less than 55 pounds on takeoff, including everything on board.",
   "Defines 'small UAS' and 'unmanned aircraft system' to include communication links and control components.",
   "Defines public aircraft, air carrier, airspace and many other aviation terms.",
   "Sets rules of construction ('shall', 'may', 'includes') for the chapter."
